ds mixture and impulse towards  confusion and impulse towards the the  the mixing of identities and so you have  a bucket of ice cream which is which is  pure let's say because it's in a  container it's closed it's also you know  being sold and by licking it or spitting  into it or whatever what you're doing is  you're defiling it and and this action  of defiling ends up being a making it  impure and you would wonder why would  anybody do that but  that is exactly what the fringe looks  like that is exactly what the edge looks  like we have a mixture of you know a  blending of gender identities a blending  of different cultural groups all these  things are happening on the edge and so  one of the things I try to help people  understand is that the way the human  person functions we function through  analogies we function through meaning  and so we can't help for these meanings  to bleed out into other phenomena and so  if on the one hand we encourage let's  say let's say something like  multiculturalism on the one hand you  know the the value behind that will also  let's say leaked out onto other  phenomena and this idea of wanting to  make something impure or wanting to to  destroy its integrity is is a almost  like a ritual version of it and what  we're seeing by people doing this  publicly and filming themselves putting  it online is a mockery or a kind of you  could call it a caricature of a magic  action or a ritual action or you know a  kind of curse or blessing a way to  affect the world because what it's doing  is it's actually affecting the world now  when you watch a video like that of  someone who is who's doing that what  it's doing is it's it's not only is it  breaking the integrity of the actual  object that they're that they're  interacting with but it's also breaking  the integrity of our actual trust in the  manner in which society works because  now the question that is going to be  asked is has anybody else done this in  the supermarket and so I'v